Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 17:06:04 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] feat(operator): the keystore agent EOA as a pure
 attestation key under a Kernel owner
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

ADAPTATION item 10 (§4 option 2). Jinn's off-chain documents (task.v1,
envelopes, captures, the legacy bridge) are raw secp256k1 signatures checked
against the address inside the document; a hardware P-256 key cannot make
them and no verifier calls ERC-1271. So the agent EOA keeps signing them --
but under config.signer it must hold no on-chain authority, which makes it
an attestation key whose compromise forges attestations, never moves funds
or rights.

- signer/attestation.ts: assertAgentEoaHasNoAuthority (refuses while the EOA
  still owns the service Safe or the agent NFT); ensureAttestationKeyBinding
  (the Kernel publishes jinn.attestationKey = <EOA> under the agent's
  ERC-8004 identity, idempotently); readAttestationKey for verifiers.
- main.ts: with config.signer the daemon refuses to boot on an unfinished
  migration and publishes the binding (non-fatal if publishing fails).
- tests: unit; in the Kernel-owner hermetic loop the check refuses before the
  Safe/NFT move and passes after, and the binding is published through
  agent-signer once and read back.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
